# Hack the Gibson commit message - Conventional Commits. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
#
#   type(scope): subject
#
# type     feat fix docs style refactor perf test build ci chore revert
# scope    types scene atlas floor render core app web ffi
#          macos linux windows ci docs
#          (omit the scope when the change is genuinely repo-wide)
# subject  imperative mood, lower case, no trailing period, 72 columns or fewer
#
# Body (optional): what changed and why, wrapped at 72 columns. The diff
# already shows what; the body is for the reasoning, and for what you checked.
#
# Breaking change footer, when other code or users must adapt:
#   BREAKING CHANGE: what breaks, and what to do instead
#
# Every line starting with '#' is stripped by git, including this one.
